{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b99f0ee0752f1f6c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Fine-grained Preference Optimization Improves Zero-shot Text-to-Speech\narXiv: 2502.02950\nAuthors: Jixun Yao, Yuguang Yang, Yu Pan, Yuan Feng, Ziqian Ning, Jianhao Ye, Hongbin Zhou, Lei Xie\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose FPO, an RL-based approach that enhances TTS robustness by optimizing specific problematic segments rather than entire utterances, leading to more data-efficient optimization.\n  2. We introduce a selective training strategy that categorizes segmental errors into temporal modeling and semantic-phonetic alignment types, applying token-level loss to resolve fine-grained issues efficiently.\n  3. Experimental results demonstrate that FPO significantly reduces bad case ratios and improves intelligibility and naturalness, achieving comparable or superior performance to baselines with considerably fewer training samples.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/功能-RL优化", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6fe9f359-dca2-4a37-92e1-5115245d58de", "uuid": "7a355437-d0a8-4ca4-b661-0b9ec07c4e0e", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T09:28:18.998Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Fine-grained Preference Optimization Improves Zero-shot Text-to-Speech\narXiv: 2502.02950\nAuthors: Jixun Yao, Yuguang Yang, Yu Pan, Yuan Feng, Ziqian Ning, Jianhao Ye, Hongbin Zhou, Lei Xie\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose FPO, an RL-based approach that enhances TTS robustness by optimizing specific problematic segments rather than entire utterances, leading to more data-efficient optimization.\n  2. We introduce a selective training strategy that categorizes segmental errors into temporal modeling and semantic-phonetic alignment types, applying token-level loss to resolve fine-grained issues efficiently.\n  3. Experimental results demonstrate that FPO significantly reduces bad case ratios and improves intelligibility and naturalness, achieving comparable or superior performance to baselines with considerably fewer training samples.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/功能-RL优化", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
