{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-af32304b1d123a85", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SwanVoice: Expressive Long-Form Zero-Shot Speech Synthesis for Both Monologue and Dialogue\narXiv: 2605.30993\nAuthors: Ruiqi Li, Yu Zhang, Changhao Pan, Ke Lei, Xiang Yin, Cheng Yang\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n===\n# CapTalk: Unified Voice Design for Single-Utterance and Dialogue Speech Generation\narXiv: 2604.08363\nAuthors: Xiaosu Su, Zihan Sun, Peilei Jia, Jun Gao\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose CapTalk, a unified caption-conditioned text-audio autoregressive framework that supports both single-utterance and dialogue voice design using utterance-level and speaker-level captions, alongside a CoT control sequence for turn-level expressive control.\n  2. We introduce a hierarchical variational conditioning mechanism with an utterance-level speaker encoder to balance stable timbre preservation and context-adaptive expression, enabling designed timbre reuse while keeping expression aligned with the current utterance and dialogue context.\n  3. We build a comprehensive evaluation protocol for both single-utterance and dialogue settings, including human evaluation for single-utterance speech and dialogue-oriented CoT prediction, controllability, and comparative evaluation.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-NL描述, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-多说话人\n===\n# Text-To-Speech with Chain-of-Details: modeling temporal dynamics in speech generation\narXiv: 2604.19330\nAuthors: Jianbo Ma, Richard Cartwright\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of the Chain-of-Details (CoD) framework that extends the coarse-to-fine generation paradigm into the temporal domain for Text-to-Speech synthesis.\n  2. Progressive refinement of temporal details across multiple stages using a cascaded architecture, with each stage targeting a specific temporal granularity.\n  3. Efficient parameter utilization across different temporal resolutions by using a shared decoder for all temporal detail predictions.\n  4. Emergent phonetic planning at the lowest temporal detail level without the need for an explicit phoneme duration predictor.\n  5. Demonstration of competitive speech synthesis performance with significantly fewer parameters compared to existing multi-stage approaches.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6fe9f359-dca2-4a37-92e1-5115245d58de", "uuid": "b55506f1-dd57-495b-b9b3-fb4e01c7a10e", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T09:28:47.677Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SwanVoice: Expressive Long-Form Zero-Shot Speech Synthesis for Both Monologue and Dialogue\narXiv: 2605.30993\nAuthors: Ruiqi Li, Yu Zhang, Changhao Pan, Ke Lei, Xiang Yin, Cheng Yang\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n===\n# CapTalk: Unified Voice Design for Single-Utterance and Dialogue Speech Generation\narXiv: 2604.08363\nAuthors: Xiaosu Su, Zihan Sun, Peilei Jia, Jun Gao\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose CapTalk, a unified caption-conditioned text-audio autoregressive framework that supports both single-utterance and dialogue voice design using utterance-level and speaker-level captions, alongside a CoT control sequence for turn-level expressive control.\n  2. We introduce a hierarchical variational conditioning mechanism with an utterance-level speaker encoder to balance stable timbre preservation and context-adaptive expression, enabling designed timbre reuse while keeping expression aligned with the current utterance and dialogue context.\n  3. We build a comprehensive evaluation protocol for both single-utterance and dialogue settings, including human evaluation for single-utterance speech and dialogue-oriented CoT prediction, controllability, and comparative evaluation.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-NL描述, TTS/控制-风格标签, TTS/功能-多说话人\n===\n# Text-To-Speech with Chain-of-Details: modeling temporal dynamics in speech generation\narXiv: 2604.19330\nAuthors: Jianbo Ma, Richard Cartwright\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of the Chain-of-Details (CoD) framework that extends the coarse-to-fine generation paradigm into the temporal domain for Text-to-Speech synthesis.\n  2. Progressive refinement of temporal details across multiple stages using a cascaded architecture, with each stage targeting a specific temporal granularity.\n  3. Efficient parameter utilization across different temporal resolutions by using a shared decoder for all temporal detail predictions.\n  4. Emergent phonetic planning at the lowest temporal detail level without the need for an explicit phoneme duration predictor.\n  5. Demonstration of competitive speech synthesis performance with significantly fewer parameters compared to existing multi-stage approaches.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
